From 252d53306578476143b8ef60c11afdd3ffa610e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:50:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): G76 threading cycle on the Fanuc Lathe post from
 a thread-cycle record

The thread kernel now carries one cl::ThreadCycle beside its explicit
passes (start, root end, major/minor diameter, lead, height, first and
minimum depth, finish allowance, infeed angle, spring passes, pull-out,
and the move span it stands for). The sim and verify keep reading the
passes; the record rides the stream as THREAD ... / THREAD END around
them and the project cache as an additive `threads` key.

A new document singleton PostOptions (undoable SetPostOptions, a
"Threading" combo under the post picker while Fanuc Lathe is chosen,
persisted as an additive `post_options` key) reaches the script as
the global `postOptions` via engine::run_with. Fanuc Lathe with
Threading = G76 writes the two-block G76 (P m r a Q dmin R d /
X Z P k Q d F lead) from the record and skips the passes; the default
stays G32, so every existing golden is byte-identical, and posts
without onThreadCycle ignore the record. Under G76, passes without a
record or a record out of range are refused by name.

Golden: crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/thread_g76.nc.
Pinned by lathe_post_g76 (golden, G32 default unchanged, stream and
project round trip, refusals, option undo) and motion
turning_thread_cycle.

Fixes #34

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
